  "notes": "Arabian Internet and Communication Services Company (trading as 'Solutions by stc', ticker 7202, a Saudi Joint Stock Company) audited consolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/2302_0_2026-02-23...). Auditor: Deloitte and Touche & Co. Chartered Accountants; unqualified opinion. The consolidated financial statements were approved by the Board of Directors at its meeting held on 27 Shaaban 1447H (corresponding to 15 February 2026) - Note 45. Amounts are presented in Saudi Riyal thousands (scale 1000) except per-share data. The statement of profit or loss, comprehensive income, financial position and changes in equity (printed FS pages 7-10) are scanned images in the filed PDF (transcribed from page renders at 2.6x); the statement of cash flows (printed page 11) and the notes (printed pages 12-62) are digital text. Consolidated group with a small non-controlling interest. There are no discontinued operations - the standard pre-tax - zakat bridge applies (income_before_income_taxes_and_zakat is the reported 'PROFIT BEFORE ZAKAT AND INCOME TAX'). The P&L presents only two operating-expense lines below gross profit: general_and_administrative_expense ('General and administration expenses') and selling_and_distribution_expense ('Selling and distribution expenses'); there is no separate depreciation line on the face of the P&L. finance_income is the reported 'Finance income'; finance_costs is 'Finance cost'; share_of_profit_associates is 'Share in net results from equity accounted investees'; other_nonoperating_expense is the reported 'Other expenses, net'. income_taxes_and_zakat is 'Zakat and income tax charge, net'. On the balance sheet: short_term_investments is 'Short term murabaha'; contract_assets and accounts_receivable ('Trade receivables') are the reported lines; prepayments is 'Prepayments and other assets'; long_term_investments is 'Non-current investments and other assets'; investments_associates is 'Investment in equity accounted investees'; intangible_assets is 'Intangible assets and goodwill'; accounts_payable is 'Trade payables, accruals and other liabilities'; contract_liabilities combines the two reported current-liability lines 'Deferred revenue' (SAR 1,878,758k; FY2024 2,089,636k) and 'Contract liabilities' (SAR 320,145k; FY2024 467,349k) - both are IFRS 15 contract liabilities; zakat_payable is 'Zakat and income tax payable'; long_term_debt / current_debt are the non-current and current portions of 'Borrowings' (Note 27); lease_liabilities_noncurrent is the reported non-current 'Lease and other liabilities' line (Note 28 - predominantly lease liabilities, also small other non-current liabilities); defined_benefit_obligation is 'End of service indemnities'; treasury_shares is the negative 'Treasury shares' line; other_reserves is the reported (negative) 'Other reserves' (Note 32 - EOSI remeasurement, share of investee OCI, share-based-payment and FX translation reserves). On the cash-flow statement: operating_cash_flow / investing_cash_flow / financing_cash_flow are the three net subtotals (operating was a net outflow in FY2025, driven by a large build-up of trade receivables and contract assets); depreciation_amortization combines the two add-back lines 'Depreciation and amortization' (SAR 254,536k; FY2024 242,657k) and 'Depreciation - right of use assets' (SAR 91,444k; FY2024 44,347k); capex is 'Purchase of property and equipment and intangible assets'; zakat_paid is 'Zakat and income taxes paid'; dividends_paid is 'Dividends paid'; lease_payments is 'Lease liabilities payments'; interest_paid is 'Finance cost paid'; debt_issued is 'Proceeds from borrowings'; debt_repaid is 'Repayment of borrowings'; foreign_exchange_effect is 'Net foreign exchange difference on cash'; the cash-flow closing balance equals the balance-sheet 'Cash and cash equivalents' line exactly. Statement page references are the printed FS page numbers: profit or loss 7, comprehensive income 8, financial position 9, changes in equity 10, cash flows 11.",
